      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"pair_id\": \"Mentuhotep|401104\", \"verdict\": \"different_name\", \"reasoning\": \"The transliteration Mnṯ.w-ḥtp.w-ꜥꜣ has three elements and the signs m, n, ṯ, w, ḥ, t, p, w, ꜥ, ꜣ. In 'Mentuhotep', M matches m, the e is an extra vowel, n matches n, t matches ṯ, u matches w, h matches ḥ, the o is an extra vowel, t matches t, and p matches p. The second w may be left out. The final ꜥꜣ has nothing to match: no letters follow the p, and a vowel letter for ꜥ or ꜣ would have to stand after the p. Record 1 is therefore only 'Mentuhotep', while record 2 is 'Mentuhotep-aa' with an extra element ꜥꜣ. The elements differ in number, so these are different names.\"}"
